SICK::Config (387 lines): the device list.

Done when:
- Moo class; load and load_string build it; path, ca, ca_name, defaults, devices, device as before;
- the file is read through Path::Tiny;
- read_secret keeps its exact message: cannot read secret file <path>: <reason of the system>. Path::Tiny has error messages of its own; the one a user sees here stays ours, and it never carries anything from the file;
- unknown keys stay an error with their path (devices.grafana: unknown key ...), in the same words: t/13-config.t pins them;
- YAML::PP stays the reader.

Config is Moo on Path::Tiny: path Str, _data (init_arg data, untyped), lazy ca/defaults/_devices/_by_name forced in BUILD in file order; load and read_secret read through Path::Tiny with our own message (path + system reason only). prove -lr t, Cisco suite green; t/e2e/run-local.sh ALL PASSED (image with libpath-tiny-perl, libtype-tiny-perl built).

